// Practice quiz: Entities and IDs
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/spring-data-jpa/entities-and-ids

::o1 constructor::Why does a JPA entity need a no-argument constructor? {
=The provider creates instances when loading rows#Correct. It then fills in the fields.
~Java requires it for all classes#Not quite. Java does not require this.
~It sets the primary key#Not quite. Generation sets the key.
~It speeds up inserts#Not quite. That is not its purpose.
}

::o1 column::Which annotation sets a database column as not nullable from the entity mapping? {
=@Column(nullable \= false)#Correct. It adds the constraint to generated DDL.
~@Id#Not quite. That marks the primary key.
~@Table#Not quite. That names the table.
~@Entity#Not quite. That marks the class as persistent.
}

::o2 id timing::With IDENTITY generation, when does a new entity get its id? {
=When the insert runs#Correct. The database generates it during the insert.
~When new is called#Not quite. A constructor does not assign one.
~When the transaction is rolled back#Not quite. Rollback does not assign ids.
~Only after a restart#Not quite. It is available right after saving.
}

::o3 save behavior::How does save decide between insert and update by default? {
=It checks whether the entity is new, usually by a null id#Correct. New means persist; otherwise merge.
~It always inserts#Not quite. It would duplicate rows.
~It always updates#Not quite. It would fail for new rows.
~It asks the caller with a parameter#Not quite. There is no such parameter.
}

::o3 equals caution::Why can equals and hashCode based on a generated id cause trouble? {
=The id is null before saving, so the hash can change#Correct. That can break hash-based collections.
~The id is a secret#Not quite. It is not a security issue here.
~Long values cannot be hashed#Not quite. They can.
~JPA forbids overriding equals#Not quite. It does not forbid that.
}

